  "result": "The file is `src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts`. It covers webhook deliveries (messages queued for a customer's receiving endpoint), and it holds both settings:\n\n- **Attempt limit:** `const MAX_ATTEMPTS = 6;` (line 22). `runWebhookDeliveryJob` marks a delivery failed with \"giving up after N attempts\" once `delivery.attempts > MAX_ATTEMPTS`.\n- **Wait growth:** `backoffMs(attempts)` (lines 90–93). There is no wait before the first try (0 attempts). After that the wait doubles each time — 1s, 2s, 4s and so on — and never goes above 5 minutes (300,000 ms).\n\nTwo files look relevant but aren't:\n- `src/config/constants.ts` has `WEBHOOK_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5`, but nothing uses it, so it has no effect.\n- `src/server/jobs/queue.ts` has its own `MAX_ATTEMPTS`/`backoffMs`, but those apply to the general in-process job queue, not to webhook delivery.\n\nANSWER: src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts",
